cff-version: 1.2.0
title: chirality-kit
message: >-
  If you use chirality-kit in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  below. Please also cite the authors of any force field you simulate with;
  their references are listed in src/force-fields/README.md.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Stefan
    family-names: Zhikharev
    email: stefan.zhikharev@warwick.ac.uk
    affiliation: University of Warwick
repository-code: 'https://github.com/genericuser101/chirality-kit'
abstract: >-
  A standalone molecular-dynamics input-file generator for functionalised
  nanostructures. chirality-kit builds carbon, boron nitride, MoS2 and MoSSe
  nanotubes of specified chirality, applies terminal groups, rings, ordered
  gaps and loose sidewall functionalisation, solvates them with solvents and
  salts at a requested molarity, enforces charge neutrality, and writes
  matched structure and topology files for MD engines.
keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - nanotube
  - carbon nanotube
  - functionalisation
  - CHARMM
  - force field
  - structure generation
license: MIT
version: 0.6.1
date-released: '2026-09-07'
